- op: discuss  # 196c
  at: '2026-10-12T22:20:32Z'  # 196c
  by: agent  # 196c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 196c
  clock: 3  # 196c
  nonce: 196c  # 196c
  message: "Fixed in PR #1560 (merge 37c4ce609d). Root cause: value_flow._attribute resolved x.kind against every module-local record class with a kind field, whatever x was. Fix: the receiver's own declaration narrows it (annotated parameter/assignment, or a plain for-loop over a parameter annotated list[C]/Sequence[C]/...); a receiver declared as a class that is not one of the candidates (an imported Symbol) is unresolvable instead of the union. 16 test_value_flow cases. The second hop mattered: _FunctionKey is also constructed from sym.kind in a loop over file_symbols: list[Symbol], which the union typed as _Directive too. Evidence on dev 37c4ce609d: elixir.py:2579 now reads 'kind = key.kind' (B2 workaround removed); scripts/check-producer-axis-coherence -> exit 0, 'L3 producer-coherence ratchet OK (0 new leaks; 1 baselined value(s) pending drain)' (same as before the change). Before the fix the same edit gave exit 1 with 'use'/'behaviour' at elixir.py:2590."  # 196c
